msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:715
msgid "Alex. I heard the gate. I hope it was you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:716
msgid "I'll tell you anyway. Somebody should know."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:718
msgid "Twenty-two days in that cage. He talked to me every night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:719
msgid "I think I was the first one who ever listened."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:722
msgid "His name is Elias Morrow. He was the quarry's chaplain."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:723
msgid "Thirty-one years ago the pit fell in. Nine men under the rock."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:724
msgid "His son Caleb was one of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:726
msgid "The town voted to seal it. Save the pass. Save the rest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:736
msgid "On the ninth day Caleb dug himself out. Blind to any light. No words left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:739
msgid "The red eyes were a lamp's lenses. The tar was pitch from the pit."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:740
msgid "The sword was the nine he couldn't dig out. And everyone since."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:743
msgid "Elias told the valley the pit had kept his boy. That it keeps everyone — if you feed it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:744
msgid "Light hurt Caleb. So every night at three, the town turned its lights off for him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:745
msgid "That's all the Veil ever was. A father who couldn't let go. A town that owed him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:746
msgid "The ones who broke went out in the Tuesday trucks. The rest stayed in the pit."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:749
msgid "The sign still says 1413. That's how many lived here the year the pit fell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:750
msgid "Elena made it her code. The one number he couldn't make smaller."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:755
msgid "Thank you for playing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:762
msgid "The broadcast reached a county trucker at 03:14. By noon, forty cars on the Old Pass."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:763
msgid "Eleven alive in the lower cells. Tomás Ruiz asked for his sister first."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:765
msgid "Grady painted a moth on the lighthouse door. Nobody has painted over it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:769
msgid "Owen, Nora, Julian and Marcus stayed. Every eye was off every door by the first frost."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:770
msgid "Elias sat with Caleb in the pit until they both went quiet. Nobody stopped him."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:773
msgid "Marcus rings the bell at dawn now. It doesn't call anyone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:777
msgid "Alex stayed. I left alone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:778
msgid "Sometimes a car stalls at the bridge, and a new eye turns up on a door at the motel."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:780
msgid "I don't read the news from Hollowmere anymore."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:785
msgid "Some of them came back to themselves. Some are under the harbor wall. We don't talk about which."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:786
msgid "Elias is still up there with his boy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/ch3_scenes_b.gd:786
msgid "Elias went down into the pit."
